--
N5008 [temp.spec.partial.match]/2, [temp.variadic]/5: matching
probe<count_of<int, int>, int, int, int> against the partial
specialization `probe<decltype(declval<f>().call(declval<Args>()...)),
Args...>' deduces Args = {int, int, int} from the trailing arguments; the
non-deduced first argument is then `decltype(f().call(int, int, int))' =
count_of<int, int>, so the specialization matches.  The front end expands
the pack in the decltype to fewer elements (the construct instantiation
in test.desc sees an empty member pack), and the
selection falls back to the primary template.  The narrower reproducer of
test.desc's remaining drop (round 163d; test.desc's assertions already
hold).  g++ 13 and clang++ 18 accept the program.  Pre-existing.
